.TH BINGUX-CONFIG 1 "2026-10-28" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-config \- read, change and check the Bingux shell configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-config
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Bingux shell keeps its settings in one TOML file,
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/bingux.toml .
.B bingux-config
reads, changes and validates it.
Editing the file by hand, running
.BR bingux\-config ,
and using Bingux Settings all go through the same validation.
Writes are atomic and keep comments and key order.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show
Print the effective configuration as TOML.
.TP
.BI get " KEY"
Print one value, for example
.BR desktop.dock_size .
.TP
.BI set " KEY VALUE"
Change one value and confirm the result.
.TP
.BI unset " KEY"
Remove a key so its default applies again.
.TP
.BI explain " KEY"
Describe a key: the accepted values, the default and the current value.
.TP
.B check
Validate the file and point at the first problem.
.TP
.B edit
Open the file in
.B $VISUAL
or
.BR $EDITOR ,
then validate it.
.TP
.B path
Print the configuration file path.
.TP
.B defaults
Print a commented file with every key at its default.
.PP
The shell and Settings also use these commands, which print one JSON object:
.TP
.B dump
The merged configuration in the shell's JSON shape.
.TP
.B save
Apply a JSON patch read from standard input.
.TP
.B import-layout
Import the runtime layout snapshot read from standard input, once.
.TP
.B wallpaper
Resolve the GNOME background to
.BR {"wallpaper":\ "file://..."} .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bingux\-config set desktop.dock_size 64
bingux\-config set search.disabled_providers '["web"]'
bingux\-config explain desktop.dock_click
bingux\-config edit
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/bingux.toml
The configuration, or
.I ~/.config/bingux/bingux.toml
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
.B 1
when a command fails or the file is invalid; the problem is printed on standard
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-settings (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/configuration.md in the Bingux source lists every key.
